# Copy to .env.local for local development. Git-ignored; never commit secrets.
#
# This file lists ONLY the NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables that frontend code actually
# reads. Today none are read: the app runs against MSW mocks (see AGENTS.md), so
# there is nothing to fill in yet.
#
# When the real Supabase client is wired up (B7) it will read, at most:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<publishable/anon key>
# Add them here only once code reads them. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is shipped
# to the browser, so only publishable values may ever live in one.
#
# NEVER put a Supabase service_role key (or any other private/server-side key)
# in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable or anywhere in this repo. `npm run test` fails if
# one appears (see src/lib/config/no-secrets.test.ts).
